WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.620
Vienna, the 1920s.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:07.450
A group of philosophers and scientists
meets with one sharp question.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.230
Which statements tell us
something about the world,

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.240
and which are nonsense?

5
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.380
In 1936, the philosopher A J Ayer
brought their test to Britain.

6
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:21.720
So could anyone ever check a
statement like God loves you?

7
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:25.250
In this mission, you'll run
sentences through Ayer's test,

8
00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:29.350
from mountains on the far side
of the moon to claims about God.

9
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.380
Then you'll follow two
travellers on one road,

10
00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.710
who disagree about where it leads.

11
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.550
Your mission: find out whether talk of
God's love could ever pass the test.
